---
/* The Atlas. The map, the panel, the filters and the overlays are the kit's
   now; what stays here is what only this archive can say — its six
   categories, the water it opens over, and the three paragraphs on how to
   read a marker. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Atlas from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/Atlas.astro";
import Sources from "../components/Sources.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import a from "../data/atlas.json";

const cats = [
  ["spine",    "The documented line",        "#A8442B"],
  ["carnia",   "Carnia — where it may start","#9A6B18"],
  ["sweep",    "Istria, where the name is",  "#1F5C6B"],
  ["other",    "Other families of the name", "#6E6A86"],
  ["senj",     "The Senj and Karlobag side", "#4E7A55"],
  ["diaspora", "Where they went",            "#2E7C8C"],
];
const overlays = [
  ["spine", "The documented descent",            "#A8442B", true],
  ["moves", "Movements — David's own arrows",    "#7A5CA8", true],
  ["areas", "The hot-spots he drew",             "#4E7A55", false],
];
const s = a.stats;
---
<Base
  title="The Atlas"
  eyebrow={`${s.places} places · ${s.people} people placed · ${s.films} register volumes`}
  dek="Every place this archive can put a person in. Click a marker and it gives you what happened there, the people the archive has standing in it, and — where the parish is on film — the register volumes themselves, open at page one.">

  <Atlas
    dataUrl={u("/atlas-data.json")}
    cats={cats}
    overlays={overlays}
    bounds={[[35, 9], [49, 26]]}
    homeLabel="Back to Istria"
    placeholder="Vodnjan · Torrington · Omiš · Broken Hill"
    hint={`${s.withPeople} of the ${s.places} places carry at least one person; ${s.withFilms} of them can hand you the register itself.`}
  >
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:6px"><strong>Movements and hot-spots are David's own</strong>, lifted whole from the Google My Map he kept for years — fifty-six arrows and ten shaded areas. They are drawn dashed and labelled as his, because <em>motion on a map is persuasive in a way that evidence is not</em>. The one journey this archive holds a document for is Zuane De Franceschi of Mione, working in the County of Pazin in 1679.</p>
  </Atlas>


  <section class="blk" style="margin-top:34px">
    <h2>Reading the map</h2>
    <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:20px">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="lab">The line is short</div>
        <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">Nine places carry the whole documented descent, and seven of them sit inside a hundred kilometres of each other. The family did not move much until 1939, and then it moved to three continents in a decade.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="lab">The cluster is not the line</div>
        <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">Rijeka, Pula and Ližnjan carry far more of the surname than Gračišće ever did — and none of them is connected to this family by any document. <strong>Weight on the map is not kinship.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="lab">The gap is the argument</div>
        <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">Between Mione in 1679 and Gologorica in 1711 there is nothing but a house with a date on it. That two-hundred-kilometre jump is the one thing this archive cannot yet prove.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="note" style="margin-top:24px"><strong>What a marker means, and what it does not.</strong> A place is on this map because a person in the roster is attached to it — by a record, a headstone, a register or a family tree. It does not mean that person was born there, and where the archive only has a parish it has used the parish. <strong>Names in three languages have been folded together</strong>: Almissa is Omiš, Vitipolis is Rijeka, Promontore is Premantura, Spalato is Split. Seventy-three entries were left off because they name a country, a region, or a church's patron saint rather than a town — those are errors in the data and are being cleaned separately.</div>
  </section>

  <Sources ids={["familysearch", "dapa", "kobler", "arolsen", "findagrave"]} />
</Base>
